# PagentOS: what happens when a scheduled unit fails (B08 req 647).
#
# Until 2026-09-13 the answer was "nothing". The nightly backup, the weekly restore drill and
# the blue/green reconcile each had a timer and no `OnFailure=`, so a failure was a line in
# the journal that nobody reads and a file that quietly stopped being updated. The owner
# would have found out about a broken backup on the day they needed it.
#
# This writes a marker the Cloud Core's `backup` health check reads, rather than calling an
# API or sending a mail. Deliberately:
#
#   * no credential. A unit that needs an owner token to report a failure is a unit that
#     needs a secret on disk, and the thing it is reporting may be the secret store itself;
#   * no network. The moment a backup fails is exactly the moment the host may be unwell,
#     and an alert that needs the API to be up cannot report that the API is down;
#   * it survives. A marker file is still there tomorrow morning, which a journal line and a
#     dropped webhook are not.
#
# Instantiated with the failing unit's name: `OnFailure=pagentos-failure-marker@%n.service`.
# %i is that name, so one template covers every scheduled unit and a unit added later gets
# reporting by adding one line to it.
#
# Read:   ls /var/lib/pagentos-backup/failures/
# Clear:  the next successful run of the unit removes its own marker.

[Unit]
Description=PagentOS: record that %i failed, where the product can see it

[Service]
Type=oneshot
Environment=PAGENTOS_BACKUP_ROOT=/var/lib/pagentos-backup
ExecStart=/bin/bash -c 'set -eu; \
  root="${PAGENTOS_BACKUP_ROOT}/failures"; mkdir -p "$root"; \
  result="$(systemctl show -p Result --value "%i" 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)"; \
  status="$(systemctl show -p ExecMainStatus --value "%i" 2>/dev/null || echo unknown)"; \
  printf "{\\"unit\\":\\"%i\\",\\"failed_at\\":\\"%%s\\",\\"result\\":\\"%%s\\",\\"exit_status\\":\\"%%s\\"}\\n" \
    "$(date -u +%%Y-%%m-%%dT%%H:%%M:%%SZ)" "$result" "$status" \
    > "$root/%i.json.next"; \
  mv "$root/%i.json.next" "$root/%i.json"'
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
